# PROPOSAL 3 — Re-typed addressbook affordance descriptor (DO NOT APPLY; review)
#
# Target (live, MUST NOT be modified by this exercise):
#   https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/meta/affordances/contact-find-by-affiliation.ttl
#   source: overlays/addressbook/affordances/contact-find-by-affiliation.ttl
#
# Audit finding addressed: WARN descriptor:untyped — catalog entry was typed
# only wiki:Affordance, escaping the prof:ResourceDescriptor contract (no
# prof:hasRole / rdfs:label / dct:conformsTo / wiki:installedBy enforced).
#
# Fix: add 'a prof:ResourceDescriptor', prof:hasRole wikirole:query-affordance
# (NEW role — see proposal-2), rdfs:label, dct:conformsTo <PROF spec>, and
# wiki:installedBy <overlay#addressbook>. The existing sh:agentInstruction and
# wiki:selectQuery are preserved verbatim. These descriptors are SPARQL query
# surfaces (selectQuery run client-side), NOT ?ext= HTTP dispatch, so they are
# modeled as wikirole:query-affordance, NOT wiki:SearchAffordance.
#
# Lands in overlays/addressbook/affordances/contact-find-by-affiliation.ttl so 'make reset'
# reproduces it; the addressbook manifest already lists this affordance.

@prefix wiki:     <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wiki#> .
@prefix sh:       <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dct:      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prof:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/dx/prof/> .
@prefix wikirole: <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wikirole#> .

</vault/meta/affordances/contact-find-by-affiliation.ttl>
    a wiki:Affordance ,
       prof:ResourceDescriptor ;
    prof:hasRole wikirole:query-affordance ;
    rdfs:label "Contact lookup by affiliation" ;
    dct:conformsTo <http://www.w3.org/TR/dx-prof/> ;
    wiki:installedBy <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/overlay#addressbook> ;
    sh:agentInstruction """
      List all Person cards affiliated with a given organization, using the
      W3C Organization Ontology membership model. Returns both current and
      historical memberships unless the caller filters by date.

      Parameter: $org — the Organization card IRI, e.g.,
      </vault/contacts/Organization/notre-dame/index.ttl#this>.

      Sources: Person card files (for org:hasMembership triples) and Membership
      card files (for org:organization triples). Both are needed because the
      membership triple may be split across card boundaries. Use Comunica
      link-traversal over the /vault/contacts/ container, or enumerate Person
      and Membership cards explicitly via LDP listing.

      Returns ?person (the Person card IRI) and ?membership (the Membership
      node IRI, which carries role/period metadata). To filter to current
      members, add: FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?membership org:memberDuring/time:hasEnd ?end }
      using the W3C Time Ontology.
    """ ;
    wiki:selectQuery """
PREFIX org: <http://www.w3.org/ns/org#>

SELECT ?person ?membership WHERE {
  ?person org:hasMembership ?membership .
  ?membership org:organization $org .
}
    """ .
